fix(block): write only actual bytes for partial last block during backup

The block uploader backupWriteProc always wrote full blockSize bytes and
advanced lastPos by the full block, even when backupReadProc read a
shorter trailing block for non-aligned volumes. This caused short writes,
incorrect progress, and duplicate tail data via copyTailData.

Track read length in readResult, use readResultWriteLength in backup and
restore write paths, and skip copyTailData when the partial block was
already written. Also fix Restore error messages that incorrectly wrapped
a stale err value.

